{"1-7":{"people":[{"id":"uzziah-h5818g","name":"Uzziah","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":3,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"amaziah-h0558g","name":"Amaziah","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":2,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"jeroboam-h3379h","name":"Jeroboam","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"jecoliah-h3203","name":"Jecoliah","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"jotham-h3147h","name":"Jotham","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":2,"firstVerse":5},{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":7}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":2}],"words":[{"base":"H5838","lemma":"עֲזַרְיָ֫הוּ","tr":"a·zar·yah","gloss":"Azariah","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":48},{"base":"H4427","lemma":"מָלַךְ","tr":"ma·lakh","gloss":"to reign","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":348},{"base":"H8141","lemma":"שָׁנָה","tr":"sha·neh","gloss":"year","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":877},{"base":"H3147","lemma":"יוֹתָם","tr":"yo·tam","gloss":"Jotham","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":24},{"base":"H0558","lemma":"אֲמַצְיָ֫הוּ","tr":"a·mats·yah","gloss":"Amaziah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":40},{"base":"H1116","lemma":"בָּמָה","tr":"ba·mah","gloss":"high place","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":102},{"base":"H2669","lemma":"חׇפְשִׁית","tr":"choph·shut","gloss":"freedom","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H3203","lemma":"יְכָלְיָהוּ","tr":"ye·khol·yah","gloss":"Jecoliah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H3389","lemma":"יְרוּשָׁלִַ֫ם, יְרוּשְׁלֵם","tr":"ye·ru·sha·laim","gloss":"Jerusalem","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":643},{"base":"H3063","lemma":"יְהוּדָה","tr":"ye·hu·dah","gloss":"Judah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":820}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"LEV","chapter":13,"verse":46,"verseEnd":46,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"As long as he has the infection, he remains unclean. He must live alone in a place outside the camp.","from":5},{"book":"NUM","chapter":12,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"As the cloud lifted from above the Tent, suddenly Miriam became leprous, white as snow. Aaron turned toward her, saw that she was leprous,","from":5},{"book":"NUM","chapter":12,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"But the LORD answered Moses, “If her father had but spit in her face, would she not have been in disgrace for seven days? Let her be confined outside the camp for seven days; after that she may be brought back in.”","from":5},{"book":"DEU","chapter":24,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"In cases of infectious skin diseases, be careful to diligently follow everything the Levitical priests instruct you. Be careful to do as I have commanded them.","from":5},{"book":"2SA","chapter":3,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"May it whirl over the heads of Joab and over the entire house of his father, and may the house of Joab never be without one having a discharge or skin disease, or one who leans on a staff or falls by the sword or lacks food.”","from":5},{"book":"2SA","chapter":8,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Thus David reigned over all Israel and administered justice and righteousness for all his people:","from":5},{"book":"2SA","chapter":15,"verse":2,"verseEnd":4,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"He would get up early and stand beside the road leading to the city gate. Whenever anyone had a grievance to bring before the king for a decision, Absalom would call out and ask, “What city are you from?” And if he replied, “Your servant is from one of the tribes of Israel,” Absalom would say, “Look, your claims are good and right, but the king has no deputy to hear you.” And he would add, “If only someone would appoint me judge in the land, then everyone with a grievance or dispute could come to me, and I would give him justice.”","from":5},{"book":"1KI","chapter":3,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Therefore give Your servant an understanding heart to judge Your people and to discern between good and evil. For who is able to govern this great people of Yours?”","from":5}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"8-15":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":5,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"uzziah-h5818g","name":"Uzziah","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":2,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"zechariah-h2148p","name":"Zechariah","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"jeroboam-h3379h","name":"Jeroboam","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"jeroboam-h3379g","name":"Jeroboam","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"nebat-h5028","name":"Nebat","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Jeroboam","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"shallum-h7967g","name":"Shallum","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":4,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"jabesh-h3003h","name":"Jabesh","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Shallum","count":3,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"jehu-h3058h","name":"Jehu","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"gadi-h1424","name":"Gadi","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Menahem","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"menahem-h4505","name":"Menahem","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":14}],"places":[{"id":"samaria-h8111","name":"Samaria","kind":"place","brief":"","count":3,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"ibleam-h2991","name":"Ibleam","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"tirzah-h8656h","name":"Tirzah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":14}],"words":[{"base":"H7967","lemma":"שַׁלּוּם","tr":"shal·lum","gloss":"Shallum","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":27},{"base":"H4427","lemma":"מָלַךְ","tr":"ma·lakh","gloss":"to reign","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":348},{"base":"H8111","lemma":"שֹׁמְרוֹן","tr":"sho·me·ron","gloss":"Samaria","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":109},{"base":"H3003","lemma":"יָבֵשׁ","tr":"ya·vesh","gloss":"Jabesh (Gilead)","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":24},{"base":"H8141","lemma":"שָׁנָה","tr":"sha·neh","gloss":"year","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":877},{"base":"H2148","lemma":"זְכַרְיָהוּ","tr":"ze·khar·yah","gloss":"Zechariah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":43},{"base":"H7194","lemma":"קָשַׁר","tr":"qa·shar","gloss":"to conspire","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":44},{"base":"H3499","lemma":"יֶ֫תֶר","tr":"ye·ter","gloss":"remainder","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":101},{"base":"H3379","lemma":"יָֽרָבְעָם","tr":"ya·rov·am","gloss":"Jeroboam","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":104},{"base":"H7970","lemma":"שְׁלֹשִׁים","tr":"she·lo·shim","gloss":"thirty","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":172}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2KI","chapter":10,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Nevertheless, the LORD said to Jehu, “Because you have done well in carrying out what is right in My sight and have done to the house of Ahab all that was in My heart, four generations of your sons will sit on the throne of Israel.”","from":12},{"book":"1KI","chapter":14,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then Jeroboamʼs wife got up and departed for Tirzah, and as soon as she stepped over the threshold of the house, the boy died.","from":14},{"book":"NUM","chapter":23,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"God is not a man, that He should lie, or a son of man, that He should change His mind. Does He speak and not act? Does He promise and not fulfill?","from":12},{"book":"1KI","chapter":14,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"As for the rest of the acts of Jeroboam, how he waged war and how he reigned, they are indeed written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel.","from":15},{"book":"1KI","chapter":14,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"As for the rest of the acts of Rehoboam, along with all that he did, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Judah?","from":15},{"book":"1KI","chapter":15,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When Baasha learned of this, he stopped fortifying Ramah and withdrew to Tirzah.","from":14},{"book":"1KI","chapter":15,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"In the third year of Asaʼs reign over Judah, Baasha killed Nadab and reigned in his place.","from":10},{"book":"1KI","chapter":15,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"In the third year of Asaʼs reign over Judah, Baasha son of Ahijah became king of all Israel, and he reigned in Tirzah twenty-four years.","from":14}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":2},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"16-22":{"people":[{"id":"menahem-h4505","name":"Menahem","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":6,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":4,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"gadi-h1424","name":"Gadi","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Menahem","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"uzziah-h5818g","name":"Uzziah","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"jeroboam-h3379g","name":"Jeroboam",