ow the evil you will do to the Israelites,” Elisha replied. “You will set fire to their fortresses, kill their young men with the sword, dash their little ones to pieces, and rip open their pregnant women.”","from":16},{"book":"RUT","chapter":2,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Now Naomi had a relative on her husbandʼs side, a prominent man of noble character from the clan of Elimelech, whose name was Boaz.","from":20},{"book":"2SA","chapter":19,"verse":32,"verseEnd":32,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Barzillai was quite old, eighty years of age, and since he was a very wealthy man, he had provided for the king while he stayed in Mahanaim.","from":20},{"book":"1KI","chapter":4,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"For Solomon had dominion over everything west of the Euphrates—over all the kingdoms from Tiphsah to Gaza—and he had peace on all sides.","from":16},{"book":"2KI","chapter":12,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So King Joash of Judah took all the sacred objects dedicated by his fathers—Jehoshaphat, Jehoram, and Ahaziah, the kings of Judah—along with his own consecrated items and all the gold found in the treasuries of the house of the LORD and the royal palace, and he sent them to Hazael king of Aram. So Hazael withdrew from Jerusalem.","from":19},{"book":"2KI","chapter":14,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"As soon as the kingdom was firmly in his grasp, Amaziah executed the servants who had murdered his father the king.","from":19},{"book":"2KI","chapter":15,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And he did evil in the sight of the LORD, as his fathers had done. He did not turn away from the sins that Jeroboam son of Nebat had caused Israel to commit.","from":18},{"book":"2KI","chapter":15,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"In the thirty-ninth year of Uzziahʼs reign over Judah, Shallum son of Jabesh became king, and he reigned in Samaria one full month.","from":17}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"23-31":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":7,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"uzziah-h5818g","name":"Uzziah","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":3,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"pekahiah-h6494","name":"Pekahiah","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"menahem-h4505","name":"Menahem","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"jeroboam-h3379g","name":"Jeroboam","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"nebat-h5028","name":"Nebat","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Jeroboam","count":2,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"pekah-h6492","name":"Pekah","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":5,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"remaliah-h7425","name":"Remaliah","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Pekah","count":3,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"argob-h0709h","name":"Argob","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"arieh-h0745","name":"Arieh","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"naphtali-h5321g","name":"Naphtali","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"tiglath-pileser-h8407","name":"Tiglath-pileser","kind":"person","brief":"Assyrian king","count":1,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"elah-h0425i","name":"Elah","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Hoshea","count":1,"firstVerse":30},{"id":"hoshea-h1954g","name":"Hoshea","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":30},{"id":"jotham-h3147h","name":"Jotham","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":30}],"places":[{"id":"samaria-h8111","name":"Samaria","kind":"place","brief":"","count":3,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"gilead-h1568g","name":"Gilead","kind":"place","brief":"In Manasseh","count":2,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"abel-beth-maacah-h0062","name":"Abel-beth-maacah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"assyria-h0804g","name":"Assyria","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"galilee-h1551","name":"Galilee","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"hazor-h2674g","name":"Hazor","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"ijon-h5859","name":"Ijon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"janoah-h3239a","name":"Janoah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"kedesh-h6943g","name":"Kedesh","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":29}],"words":[{"base":"H6492","lemma":"פֶּ֫קַח","tr":"pe·qach","gloss":"Pekah","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":11},{"base":"H8141","lemma":"שָׁנָה","tr":"sha·neh","gloss":"year","lang":"h","inPassage":7,"uses":877},{"base":"H0062","lemma":"אָבֵל בֵּית־מֲעַכָה","tr":"a·vel bet-ma·a·khah","gloss":"Abel-beth-maachah","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":12},{"base":"H7425","lemma":"רְמַלְיָ֜הוּ","tr":"re·mal·ya·hu","gloss":"Remaliah","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":13},{"base":"H4427","lemma":"מָלַךְ","tr":"ma·lakh","gloss":"to reign","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":348},{"base":"H6494","lemma":"פְּקַחְיָה","tr":"pe·qach·yah","gloss":"Pekahiah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":3},{"base":"H8111","lemma":"שֹׁמְרוֹן","tr":"sho·me·ron","gloss":"Samaria","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":109},{"base":"H2572","lemma":"חֲמִשִּׁים","tr":"cha·mish·shim","gloss":"fifty","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":163},{"base":"H8407","lemma":"תִּגְלַת פִּלְאֶ֫סֶר","tr":"tig·lat pil·e·ser","gloss":"Tiglath-pileser","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":12},{"base":"H5028","lemma":"נְבָט","tr":"ne·vat","gloss":"Nebat","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":25}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1CH","chapter":5,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"So the God of Israel stirred up the spirit of Pul king of Assyria (that is, Tiglath-pileser king of Assyria) to take the Reubenites, the Gadites, and the half-tribe of Manasseh into exile. And he brought them to Halah, Habor, Hara, and the river of Gozan, where they remain to this day.","from":29},{"book":"2KI","chapter":17,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"In the ninth year of Hoshea, the king of Assyria captured Samaria and carried away the Israelites to Assyria, where he settled them in Halah, in Gozan by the Habor River, and in the cities of the Medes.","from":29},{"book":"LEV","chapter":26,"verse":32,"verseEnd":32,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And I will lay waste the land, so that your enemies who dwell in it will be appalled.","from":29},{"book":"LEV","chapter":26,"verse":38,"verseEnd":39,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"You will perish among the nations, and the land of your enemies will consume you. Those of you who survive in the lands of your enemies will waste away in their iniquity and will decay in the sins of their fathers.","from":29},{"book":"NUM","chapter":32,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Now the Reubenites and Gadites, who had very large herds and flocks, surveyed the lands of Jazer and Gilead, and they saw that the region was suitable for livestock.","from":29},{"book":"NUM","chapter":32,"verse":40,"verseEnd":40,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So Moses gave Gilead to the clan of Machir son of Manasseh, and they settled there.","from":29},{"book":"DEU","chapter":3,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"To Machir I gave Gilead,","from":29},{"book":"DEU","chapter":4,"verse":26,"verseEnd":27,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"I call heaven and earth as witnesses against you this day that you will quickly perish from the land that you are crossing the Jordan to possess. You will not live long upon it, but will be utterly destroyed. Then the LORD will scatter you among the peoples, and only a few of you will survive among the nations to which the LORD will drive you.","from":29}],"notes":[{"id":"isa-7-damascus-samaria","title":"The two kings who threatened Ahaz","kind":"prophecy"}],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3}]},"32-38":{"people":[{"id":"jotham-h3147h","name":"Jotham","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":3,"firstVerse":32},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":3,"firstVerse":32},{"id":"pekah-h6492","name":"Pekah","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":32},{"id":"remaliah-h7425","name":"Remaliah","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Pekah","count":2,"firstVerse":32},{"id":"uzziah-h5818g","name":"Uzziah","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":2,"firstVerse":32},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":32},{"id":"jerusha-h3388","name":"Jerusha","kind":"person","brief":"Daughter of Zadok","count":1,"firstVerse":33},{"id":"zadok-h6659h","name":"Zadok","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Jerusha","count":1,"firstVerse":33},{"id":"rezin-h7526g","name":"Rezin","kind":"person","brief":"Syrian king","count":1,"firstVerse":37},{"id":"ahaz-h0271g","name":"Ahaz","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":38},{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":38}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":33},{"id":"syria-h0758i","name":"Syria","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":37}],"words":[{"base":"H3147","lemma":"יוֹתָם","tr":"yo·tam","gloss":"Jotham","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":24},{"base":"H4427","lemma":"מָלַךְ","tr":"ma·lakh","gloss":"to reign","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":348},{"base":"H6492","lemma":"פֶּ֫קַח","tr":"pe·qach","gloss":"Pekah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":11},{"base":"H7425","lemma":"רְמַלְיָ֜הוּ","tr":"re·mal·ya·hu","gloss":"Remaliah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":13},{"base":"H5818","lemma":"עֻזִּיָּהוּ","tr":"uz·ziy·yah","gloss":"Uzziah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":27},{"base":"H3063","lemma":"יְהוּדָה","tr":"ye·hu·dah","gloss":"Judah","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":820},{"base":"H1116","lemma":"בָּמָה","tr":"ba·mah","gloss":"high place","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":102},{"base":"H8141","lemma":"שָׁנָה","tr":"sha·neh","gloss":"year","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":877},{"base":"H3388","lemma":"יְרוּשָׁא, יְרוּשָׁה","tr":"ye·ru·sah","gloss":"Jerusha","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H1992","lemma":"הֵ֫מָּה","tr":"hem·mah","gloss":"they(masc.)","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":552}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2KI","chapter":16,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then Rezin king of Aram and Pekah son of Remaliah king of Israel came up to wage war against Jerusalem. They besieged Ahaz but could not overcome him.","from":37},{"book":"ISA","chapter":7,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Now in the days that Ahaz son of Jotham, the son of Uzziah, was king of Judah, Rezin king of Aram marched up to wage war against Jerusalem. He was accompanied by Pekah son of Remaliah the king of Israel, but he could not overpower the city.","from":37},{"book":"DEU","chapter":28,"verse":48,"verseEnd":48,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"you will serve your enemies the LORD will send against you in famine, thirst, nakedness, and destitution. He will place an iron yoke on your neck until He has destroyed you.","from":37},{"book":"1SA","chapter":3,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"On that day I will carry out against Eli everything I have spoken about his house, from beginning to end.","from":37},{"book":"2SA","chapter":7,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And when your days are fulfilled and you rest with your fathers, I will raise up your descendant after you, who will come from your own body, and I will establish his kingdom.","from":38},{"book":"1KI","chapter":1,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So his servants said to him, “Let us search for a young virgin for our lord the king, to attend to him and care for him and lie by his side to keep him warm.”","from":38},{"book":"1KI","chapter":14,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And the length of Jeroboamʼs reign was twenty-two years, and he rested with his fathers, and his son Nadab reigned in his place.","from":38},{"book":"1KI","chapter":14,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And Rehoboam rested with his fathers and was buried with them in the City of David; his motherʼs name was Naamah the Ammonite. And his son Abijam reigned in his place.","from":38}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":2},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]}}